1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Downloaded from
YTS.BZ

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Official YIFY movies site:
YTS.BZ

3
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:46,125
[gentle music playing]

4
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:57,750
[Ry] <i>My body has become my enemy.</i>

5
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:03,125
<i>But here I am,
just another particle of the Earth.</i>

6
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:07,082
<i>The ocean doesn't care about sickness</i>

7
00:01:07,083 --> 00:01:09,957
<i>or life and death.</i>

8
00:01:09,958 --> 00:01:12,791
<i>It doesn't care for
our struggles or our pain.</i>

9
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:17,375
<i>Or that I would have given everything...</i>

10
00:01:18,666 --> 00:01:20,791
<i>...for one last summer like this.</i>

11
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:24,333
<i>One last sunrise...</i>

12
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:27,041
<i>...with him.</i>

13
00:01:30,166 --> 00:01:32,125
{\an8}[♪ Kye Kye sings "People"]

14
00:01:36,458 --> 00:01:39,000
♪ ♪

15
00:02:01,791 --> 00:02:04,415
<i>♪ I still yearn to be ♪</i>

16
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:07,082
<i>♪ love without a need to please ♪</i>

17
00:02:07,083 --> 00:02:08,916
<i>♪ Help me, help me ♪</i>

18
00:02:11,666 --> 00:02:15,290
{\an8}<i>♪ Silent crave to have childish peace ♪</i>

19
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:17,082
<i>♪ while weary things ♪</i>

20
00:02:17,083 --> 00:02:19,040
- [ears ringing, heart beating]
- <i>♪ haunt me, haunt me ♪</i>

21
00:02:19,041 --> 00:02:21,457
- <i>♪ Like falling in my sleep...</i>
- [breathes shakily]

22
00:02:21,458 --> 00:02:23,540
[music continues low and distorted]

23
00:02:23,541 --> 00:02:26,083
[shallow gasping]

24
00:02:27,166 --> 00:02:29,457
Ry. Ry.

25
00:02:29,458 --> 00:02:31,415
- [shallow gasping continues]
- [heart beating faster]

26
00:02:31,416 --> 00:02:34,207
[tense music playing]

27
00:02:34,208 --> 00:02:36,332
Ry!

28
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:37,624
Move, move, move!

29
00:02:37,625 --> 00:02:39,165
I got her. Okay.

30
00:02:39,166 --> 00:02:40,290
Okay, breathe.

31
00:02:40,291 --> 00:02:42,583
Breathe, Ry.
You got to breathe, sweetheart.

32
00:02:46,041 --> 00:02:49,374
At this stage, Oriah,
I would strongly recommend surgery.

33
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:51,790
{\an8}There's still a chance
we can remove all the tubers,

34
00:02:51,791 --> 00:02:54,332
{\an8}and you could be seizure-free.

35
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:57,166
{\an8}And there's an equal chance
that I'll lose my memory.

36
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:02,749
{\an8}People, places, how to walk,
how to dance, how to live.

37
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:05,374
Everything that makes me a person.

38
00:03:05,375 --> 00:03:07,207
Ry, this is your life we're talking about.

39
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:09,957
Exactly, Mom. It's my life.

40
00:03:09,958 --> 00:03:12,124
{\an8}Okay, we could increase the medication,

41
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:14,790
{\an8}but it'll most likely increase
the side effects.

42
00:03:14,791 --> 00:03:16,832
{\an8}I would set alarms
so you don't miss a dose,

43
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,165
{\an8}or they won't work properly.

44
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,083
{\an8}Can you commit to that?

45
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:25,333
Ry. Ry.

46
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,957
Honey, I know they make you
feel like shit.

47
00:03:30,958 --> 00:03:32,624
{\an8}Correction.

48
00:03:32,625 --> 00:03:34,790
{\an8}They don't let me feel anything.

49
00:03:34,791 --> 00:03:36,915
All right, Lena, be sure to book a driver
to take her

50
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:38,665
- wherever she wants to go.
- Yeah.

51
00:03:38,666 --> 00:03:41,499
Also, there's a pharmacy
two streets over from the hotel

52
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,457
where you can fill her prescription.

53
00:03:43,458 --> 00:03:45,165
Other than that,
it's just the usual things

54
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:46,665
{\an8}we need to be mindful of
with her epilepsy:

55
00:03:46,666 --> 00:03:48,957
{\an8}flashing lights, get good sleep,

56
00:03:48,958 --> 00:03:50,957
no stress, no alcohol.

57
00:03:50,958 --> 00:03:53,541
Great. The nuns and I will be having
our hot girl summer.

58
00:03:54,708 --> 00:03:57,082
So, days one through four are super busy

59
00:03:57,083 --> 00:03:59,499
with the location manager
and Redwyn attorneys.

60
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,874
I'll try to schedule some time off, but--

61
00:04:01,875 --> 00:04:03,333
What about spending time together?

62
00:04:05,541 --> 00:04:07,249
Mom, you promised to show me
where you grew up.

63
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:10,999
No, honey, we are gonna spend
lots of time together.

64
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,457
We have six whole weeks.

65
00:04:12,458 --> 00:04:14,540
We're gonna have fun. It's Mallorca.

66
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:16,583
As long as you keep your promise.

67
00:04:28,458 --> 00:04:30,665
Thank you.

68
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:32,374
All right, let me see that schedule again.

69
00:04:32,375 --> 00:04:33,665
[Lena] Yes.

70
00:04:33,666 --> 00:04:36,000
{\an8}[♪ Sofia Kourtesis sings "Madres"]

71
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,458
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

72
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,708
[tires screech]

73
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:56,708
♪ ♪

74
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,374
<i>Hola.</i>

75
00:05:15,375 --> 00:05:16,833
[hotel manager] Welcome.

76
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:20,165
We're expecting you, Miss Pera.

77
00:05:20,166 --> 00:05:22,374
- Oh, call me Isolde. Hi.
- Welcome.

78
00:05:22,375 --> 00:05:24,707
<i>Muchas gracias.</i> Thank you.

79
00:05:24,708 --> 00:05:27,582
This is my daughter Oriah. Honey.

80
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:28,874
- Hi.
- She's a bit jet-lagged.

81
00:05:28,875 --> 00:05:30,540
- Hi.
- Why don't you get settled,

82
00:05:30,541 --> 00:05:32,249
and I'll meet you in the room, okay?

83
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:33,790
I have a quick conference call.

84
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,624
[hotel manager] Our concierge team
is looking forward

85
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:36,791
<i>- to meeting you.</i>
- [indistinct chatter]

86
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:40,957
[Amara German accent] Hi there,

87
00:05:40,958 --> 00:05:42,290
and welcome to our hotel.

88
00:05:42,291 --> 00:05:44,540
- Hi.
- How was your flight?

89
00:05:44,541 --> 00:05:46,249
- It was fine.
- Good.

90
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:48,665
Oh, sorry, you have a little something.

91
00:05:48,666 --> 00:05:50,249
Ah! [chuckles]

92
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:53,124
I saw it on TikTok.
This took me 20 minutes.

93
00:05:53,125 --> 00:05:54,957
Tell me, honestly,

94
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:57,583
is it worth investing the time
on the other eye?

95
00:05:58,625 --> 00:06:01,499
Given it's company time,
I'd say yes. [chuckles]

96
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,624
Mm. I like you.

97
00:06:03,625 --> 00:06:05,124
Follow me. Right,
I'll show you to your room.

98
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:06,290
This way.

99
00:06:06,291 --> 00:06:08,207
- [Amara] I'm Amara, by the way.
- [Ry] I'm Ry.

100
00:06:08,208 --> 00:06:10,415
[Amara] Okay, so this is the lobby.

101
00:06:10,416 --> 00:06:11,874
You can come find me here
anytime you need.

102
00:06:11,875 --> 00:06:15,290
So, what brings you
to our Spanish paradise?

103
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:18,040
- My mom's closing a real estate deal.
- Uh-huh?

104
00:06:18,041 --> 00:06:20,040
Yeah, her company wants
to build a new hotel.

105
00:06:20,041 --> 00:06:22,665
[gasps] Ooh, another hotel. How exciting.

106
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:24,582
The locals are gonna love that.

107
00:06:24,583 --> 00:06:25,999
Do you know the island at all?

108
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,249
No. No, it's my first time.

109
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:30,124
I haven't really been out of Texas much.

110
00:06:30,125 --> 00:06:33,165
Wow, a Texan. How exotic.

111
00:06:33,166 --> 00:06:36,832
So, Ry, what do you like to do for fun?

112
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:38,040
Oh, I don't know.

113
00:06:38,041 --> 00:06:40,499
Maybe go to the beach or lie by the pool.

114
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,957
You can definitely do that,
but there's tons of other stuff.

115
00:06:43,958 --> 00:06:45,957
- Do you like caves?
- Caves?

116
00:06:45,958 --> 00:06:47,207
[Amara] <i>Are you single?</i>

117
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:49,915
- Yeah.
- Ugh, the locals here are superhot.

118
00:06:49,916 --> 00:06:52,999
They're like this crazy mix
of Carthaginians, then Romans,

119
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,165
then the Catalan settlers
from France and Spain.

120
00:06:55,166 --> 00:06:58,665
Whatever you are into,
it's like a hookup buffet.

121
00:06:58,666 --> 00:07:01,582
Oh, and don't be surprised
if you see goats in trees.

122
00:07:01,583 --> 00:07:03,790
- Goats in trees?
- Yes, goats in trees.

123
00:07:03,791 --> 00:07:04,999
Anyway, the point is,

124
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,582
you're going to have a summer
worth remembering.

125
00:07:07,583 --> 00:07:09,540
Okay, your mother's room
is just across the hall,

126
00:07:09,541 --> 00:07:11,541
and this one's you.

127
00:07:12,916 --> 00:07:14,916
[gentle music playing]

128
00:07:17,958 --> 00:07:20,625
Your mother's company built
an amazing place.

129
00:07:22,083 --> 00:07:23,333
Yeah.

130
00:07:25,458 --> 00:07:27,790
[phone alarm beeping and vibrating]

131
00:07:27,791 --> 00:07:29,624
Sorry.

132
00:07:29,625 --> 00:07:31,624
- [alarm stops]
- I'll let you settle in.

133
00:07:31,625 --> 00:07:33,957
Just give us a call downstairs
if you need anything at all.

134
00:07:33,958 --> 00:07:35,374
<i>Auf Wiedersehen.</i> Bye-bye.

135
00:07:35,375 --> 00:07:37,750
- Thank you, Amara.
- [door closes]

136
00:07:47,666 --> 00:07:49,208
[pills rattle]

137
00:07:57,125 --> 00:07:58,291
[bottle closes]

138
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:01,915
- [waves rolling]
- [seagulls calling]

139
00:08:01,916 --> 00:08:03,915
[Ry] So, what's the plan for tomorrow?

140
00:08:03,916 --> 00:08:05,207
[Isolde] I'm packed.

141
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:08,291
I have back-to-back meetings
and party planning.

142
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:10,332
What party?

143
00:08:10,333 --> 00:08:12,374
A fundraiser.

144
00:08:12,375 --> 00:08:15,332
Yeah. In addition to getting them
to let us build the hotel,

145
00:08:15,333 --> 00:08:17,582
in good faith,
we are building an arts center

146
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:20,124
- for the children of Mallorca.
- That's nice.

147
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,291
[phone chimes]

148
00:08:24,041 --> 00:08:25,665
Everything okay?

149
00:08:25,666 --> 00:08:27,999
Just the-the company. [sighs]

150
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,166
They're checking in
to see if I'll return this fall.

151
00:08:31,208 --> 00:08:32,874
But you are going back, right?

152
00:08:32,875 --> 00:08:35,040
You just need to rest this summer.

153
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:36,833
And then you're gonna be
back in the saddle.

154
00:08:38,541 --> 00:08:40,208
Yeah.

155
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,540
[Chloe over phone] <i>We're all going out
tonight to celebrate</i>

156
00:08:43,541 --> 00:08:44,832
<i>the end of the season.</i>

157
00:08:44,833 --> 00:08:46,290
<i>We wish you were here.</i>

158
00:08:46,291 --> 00:08:47,665
<i>How are you feeling?</i>

159
00:08:47,666 --> 00:08:49,207
<i>Is the new medication helping?</i>

160
00:08:49,208 --> 00:08:52,040
Uh, it's... [chuckles]
it's an adjustment for sure.

161
00:08:52,041 --> 00:08:54,749
<i>We've all been so worried about you.</i>

162
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:57,499
First of all, don't do that.

163
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,332
Second, I am fine.

164
00:08:59,333 --> 00:09:02,874
My mom has this whole thing
planned for tomorrow.

165
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:05,082
She's gonna show me where she grew up.

166
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:06,624
<i>Your mom is such a queen.</i>

167
00:09:06,625 --> 00:09:07,707
<i>And forget what I said.</i>

168
00:09:07,708 --> 00:09:09,832
<i>I wish we were all there with you guys.</i>

169
00:09:09,833 --> 00:09:10,874
Mm-hmm.

170
00:09:10,875 --> 00:09:12,332
<i>Well, tell me
if you see any hot Spaniards.</i>

171
00:09:12,333 --> 00:09:14,082
<i>- Okay?</i>
- Yeah. For sure.

172
00:09:14,083 --> 00:09:15,832
<i>- We love you, babes. Call me!</i>
- [chuckles]

173
00:09:15,833 --> 00:09:17,832
- [women] <i>See you, Ry!
- Love you.</i>

174
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,833
- Love you. Bye.
- [women] <i>Bye.</i>

175
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:25,415
[phone alarm beeping and vibrating]

176
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:27,207
- [sighs]
- [alarm stops]

177
00:09:27,208 --> 00:09:29,208
[gentle guitar music playing]

178
00:09:30,291 --> 00:09:31,708
[sputters lips]

179
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:45,000
♪ ♪

180
00:09:49,375 --> 00:09:51,333
[splashing and laughter in distance]

181
00:09:53,083 --> 00:09:56,125
[splashing and laughter continue]

182
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[guard] Hey! [shouts in Spanish]

183
00:10:02,375 --> 00:10:04,333
[urgent Spanish chatter]

184
00:10:10,666 --> 00:10:13,582
[birds chirping]

185
00:10:13,583 --> 00:10:16,665
[Isolde] Okay, so we have
around 150 guests.

186
00:10:16,666 --> 00:10:17,915
Ooh, this is pretty.

187
00:10:17,916 --> 00:10:22,582
Hey, Ry, do you like eggshell or oatmeal?

188
00:10:22,583 --> 00:10:24,540
Why do they all have to be
named after food?

189
00:10:24,541 --> 00:10:26,375
[Isolde] I don't know.

190
00:10:27,416 --> 00:10:29,415
[sighs] Honey, why don't you go
do something fun,

191
00:10:29,416 --> 00:10:31,416
and I'll meet up with you later.

192
00:10:32,416 --> 00:10:34,249
- I was gonna hit the beach.
- Well, that's a good idea.

193
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:36,415
Take the driver. Oh!

194
00:10:36,416 --> 00:10:38,749
And extra meds. And water.

195
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:40,249
And put some sunblock, sweetheart.

196
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:42,915
- Oh, and, Ry--
- Be careful?

197
00:10:42,916 --> 00:10:44,875
Have fun.

198
00:10:46,791 --> 00:10:48,290
Coconut cream for the win.

199
00:10:48,291 --> 00:10:49,999
[footsteps departing]

200
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,290
See? Pretends not to care, but she does.

201
00:10:52,291 --> 00:10:53,666
Hmm.

202
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:59,999
- Hi.
- Hi.

203
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,582
Slow morning, was it?

204
00:11:01,583 --> 00:11:03,415
Why?

205
00:11:03,416 --> 00:11:04,499
[chuckles] Your eyes.

206
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,124
- Oh.
- I love the eyeliner.

207
00:11:06,125 --> 00:11:07,249
- Thank you.
- [chuckles]

208
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:08,915
So, where to?

209
00:11:08,916 --> 00:11:12,874
Oh, actually, yes, I was gonna ask you
if you had any beach recommendations.

210
00:11:12,875 --> 00:11:15,499
I think I know just the spot.

211
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,790
- It's a real hidden gem.
- Ooh.

212
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:19,125
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

213
00:11:20,166 --> 00:11:21,915
Perfect.

214
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:24,500
[♪ Bad Bunny and The Marias
sing "Otro Atardecer"]

215
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:36,791
♪ ♪

216
00:11:43,125 --> 00:11:45,083
[quiet chatter]

217
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:56,375
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

218
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:20,125
♪ ♪

219
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:49,416
♪ ♪

220
00:12:58,416 --> 00:13:00,416
[song fades]

221
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:07,208
[quiet chatter]

222
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:35,333
[laughter in distance]

223
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:41,083
[laughter continues]

224
00:13:45,958 --> 00:13:47,207
[sighs heavily]

225
00:13:47,208 --> 00:13:50,000
["Otro Atardecer" resumes
with lyrics in Spanish]

226
00:14:03,166 --> 00:14:04,583
[laughs]

227
00:14:06,291 --> 00:14:09,000
- [song fades]
- [laughter, quiet chatter]

228
00:14:10,041 --> 00:14:12,041
[gentle music playing]

229
00:14:36,708 --> 00:14:38,958
♪ ♪

230
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:53,166
[music fades]

231
00:14:55,666 --> 00:14:57,666
Can I help you?

232
00:14:58,875 --> 00:15:02,416
Uh... um, no, no.

233
00:15:03,416 --> 00:15:04,707
It's rude to stare, <i>señorita.</i>

234
00:15:04,708 --> 00:15:06,332
I wasn't... I wasn't staring.

235
00:15:06,333 --> 00:15:08,249
I was just, uh, uh...

236
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:10,166
I was looking behind you.

237
00:15:11,791 --> 00:15:14,166
[Julian] Wow. Nice view.

238
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:18,374
[chuckles nervously]
Okay, well, I'm gonna go.

239
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:20,624
- Yeah, you should go.
- Excuse me?

240
00:15:20,625 --> 00:15:22,999
I said that you should go.

241
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,499
Did I do something?
Uh, do you have a problem?

242
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,249
I do have a problem.

243
00:15:27,250 --> 00:15:29,665
This is a locals' beach.

244
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:32,957
We prefer when tourists don't
stare at us while we sunbathe.

245
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:34,165
Uh, I'm so sorry.

246
00:15:34,166 --> 00:15:35,332
I hadn't realized
it was a locals-only beach.

247
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:36,457
I just wanted to swim.

248
00:15:36,458 --> 00:15:38,374
Well, I think you might find the pool

249
00:15:38,375 --> 00:15:41,374
