00:27:59,916 --> 00:28:02,374
- [Amara] Yes, Ry!
- [Sofia] Okay.

506
00:28:02,375 --> 00:28:03,999
- Oh, my God!
- Let's do it!

507
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,290
- This is great.
- [gasps]

508
00:28:05,291 --> 00:28:07,707
[indistinct chatter continues]

509
00:28:07,708 --> 00:28:10,749
Oh! Yes, baby. Work it.

510
00:28:10,750 --> 00:28:12,582
<i>♪ Uh-huh, uh-huh, uh ♪</i>

511
00:28:12,583 --> 00:28:14,582
<i>♪ Uh-huh, uh-huh...</i>

512
00:28:14,583 --> 00:28:16,457
Okay, are you coming? Ry!

513
00:28:16,458 --> 00:28:18,415
[♪ Astroboyz sing "Se Menea"]

514
00:28:18,416 --> 00:28:20,625
- [crowd cheering]
- [song continues in Spanish]

515
00:28:23,916 --> 00:28:25,915
- Ah!
- I tried to order three.

516
00:28:25,916 --> 00:28:27,707
- [Amara] Wow!
- [Sofia] Yes, girl!

517
00:28:27,708 --> 00:28:30,207
- But you need to work on your Spanish.
- Oh! We're gonna do shots!

518
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:32,915
<i>- Un, dos, tres.</i>
- Cheers.

519
00:28:32,916 --> 00:28:34,000
Cheers.

520
00:28:34,916 --> 00:28:36,582
Mm.

521
00:28:36,583 --> 00:28:38,415
- Mm.
- [exclaims]

522
00:28:38,416 --> 00:28:40,332
[groans]

523
00:28:40,333 --> 00:28:41,415
- Gosh.
- Oh, Julian!

524
00:28:41,416 --> 00:28:42,582
Come have a shot.

525
00:28:42,583 --> 00:28:44,332
Ry ordered enough for everyone.

526
00:28:44,333 --> 00:28:45,457
[Julian] Hello, girls.

527
00:28:45,458 --> 00:28:47,833
Hello, big spender.

528
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:51,249
[Amara] I love this song.

529
00:28:51,250 --> 00:28:53,582
Ooh! Who wants to dance?

530
00:28:53,583 --> 00:28:55,499
- [Sofia] Me!
- [Amara] Ry?

531
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:56,499
[Ry groans]

532
00:28:56,500 --> 00:28:57,749
Come on, <i>chica.</i>

533
00:28:57,750 --> 00:29:00,333
Let's see what you got, Miss America.

534
00:29:01,375 --> 00:29:03,874
[Amara] Let's go, baby.

535
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:05,415
- [Ry] I'll come with you.
- [Sofia] Ignore him.

536
00:29:05,416 --> 00:29:07,458
<i>¡Venga, venga!</i>

537
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:14,958
[♪ Kinski Gallo sings "Me Gusta"]

538
00:29:18,458 --> 00:29:21,458
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

539
00:29:46,958 --> 00:29:49,750
♪ ♪

540
00:30:14,625 --> 00:30:15,708
[Ry] Stop.

541
00:30:17,833 --> 00:30:19,082
Dude, get off me.

542
00:30:19,083 --> 00:30:21,666
♪ ♪

543
00:30:28,791 --> 00:30:30,750
[crowd cheering]

544
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:45,749
[song distorting]

545
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:47,040
[audio muffled]

546
00:30:47,041 --> 00:30:49,000
Hey. [muffled shout]

547
00:30:51,041 --> 00:30:52,582
I got you.

548
00:30:52,583 --> 00:30:55,124
[audio continues clearly]

549
00:30:55,125 --> 00:30:56,291
[panting] Okay.

550
00:31:01,541 --> 00:31:03,749
[sighs] You sure you're okay?

551
00:31:03,750 --> 00:31:04,999
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

552
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,915
I'm fine. I just...

553
00:31:06,916 --> 00:31:08,707
[chuckles] I just can't drink tequila.

554
00:31:08,708 --> 00:31:10,207
Maybe there was something in your drink.

555
00:31:10,208 --> 00:31:11,458
No, no. I'm okay.

556
00:31:13,708 --> 00:31:16,249
Okay, good, 'cause we got to go.

557
00:31:16,250 --> 00:31:18,375
- What?
- Put this on.

558
00:31:19,416 --> 00:31:21,957
- Are we running from people?
- I'll explain later.

559
00:31:21,958 --> 00:31:23,540
I've never ridden a motorcycle.

560
00:31:23,541 --> 00:31:24,915
Oh, really?

561
00:31:24,916 --> 00:31:26,457
Don't worry, you're gonna love it.

562
00:31:26,458 --> 00:31:28,332
[engine starts]

563
00:31:28,333 --> 00:31:31,333
[♪ Karol G sings "Tus Gafitas"]

564
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,000
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

565
00:31:59,458 --> 00:32:00,999
You okay?

566
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:02,041
I'm good.

567
00:32:05,708 --> 00:32:07,666
♪ ♪

568
00:32:28,416 --> 00:32:30,416
I want to show you somewhere.

569
00:32:32,666 --> 00:32:34,165
[song ends]

570
00:32:34,166 --> 00:32:36,165
- You're a fisherman?
- Mm-hmm.

571
00:32:36,166 --> 00:32:38,625
- [chuckles]
- It's my family business.

572
00:32:39,666 --> 00:32:41,165
I grew up on the water.

573
00:32:41,166 --> 00:32:42,416
It's what I know.

574
00:32:44,500 --> 00:32:46,833
One day, I'll take over the fishery
from my dad.

575
00:32:47,875 --> 00:32:50,707
- Hopefully.
- Hopefully?

576
00:32:50,708 --> 00:32:54,582
The fisheries on our island are suffering
because of the tourists

577
00:32:54,583 --> 00:32:59,290
and the commercial companies
are hurting the island.

578
00:32:59,291 --> 00:33:03,708
On the other hand,
it's surviving because of them.

579
00:33:05,333 --> 00:33:10,083
So now you know why I never buy
any of those "I heart Mallorca" shirts.

580
00:33:12,041 --> 00:33:14,957
More people could mean progress.

581
00:33:14,958 --> 00:33:16,332
Mm. [sighs]

582
00:33:16,333 --> 00:33:21,749
Destroying family businesses
doesn't feel like progress.

583
00:33:21,750 --> 00:33:22,833
Mm.

584
00:33:25,291 --> 00:33:27,207
So what about you?

585
00:33:27,208 --> 00:33:30,207
What's waiting for you back in Texas?

586
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:31,583
[chuckles]

587
00:33:32,791 --> 00:33:34,415
I'm a dancer.

588
00:33:34,416 --> 00:33:35,874
Exotic?

589
00:33:35,875 --> 00:33:37,665
[both chuckle]

590
00:33:37,666 --> 00:33:40,749
- I'm with a company. [chuckles]
- Okay, okay.

591
00:33:40,750 --> 00:33:42,749
But...

592
00:33:42,750 --> 00:33:45,041
I don't even know if I'm going back.

593
00:33:48,250 --> 00:33:51,749
My life back home
just feels like a constant...

594
00:33:51,750 --> 00:33:53,749
loop. [sighs]

595
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:56,707
Dance is the only thing
that gives it meaning.

596
00:33:56,708 --> 00:33:58,041
And gives me some freedom.

597
00:33:59,458 --> 00:34:00,749
Then why stop?

598
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:02,583
'Cause it's not up to me anymore.

599
00:34:03,625 --> 00:34:06,082
I'm sorry. My problems
probably sound so trivial.

600
00:34:06,083 --> 00:34:07,374
No, no, no, it's okay.

601
00:34:07,375 --> 00:34:09,332
I mean, rich girls can be sad, too.

602
00:34:09,333 --> 00:34:11,749
We should put that on a T-shirt.

603
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:13,249
Yeah, we should do that.

604
00:34:13,250 --> 00:34:15,457
[laughs] What are you doing?

605
00:34:15,458 --> 00:34:16,874
Come on.

606
00:34:16,875 --> 00:34:18,207
I can help you if you can't swim.

607
00:34:18,208 --> 00:34:20,083
- I can swim.
- [water splashing]

608
00:34:23,666 --> 00:34:25,625
[gentle music playing]

609
00:34:27,708 --> 00:34:29,041
[chuckles]

610
00:34:30,791 --> 00:34:31,958
[chuckles]

611
00:34:36,583 --> 00:34:38,124
[both chuckle]

612
00:34:38,125 --> 00:34:40,999
See? I'm a great swimmer.

613
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:43,665
I just wanted to make you take
your clothes off this time.

614
00:34:43,666 --> 00:34:45,666
[both laughing]

615
00:34:47,791 --> 00:34:49,124
Oh.

616
00:34:49,125 --> 00:34:50,832
Okay, truce, truce.

617
00:34:50,833 --> 00:34:51,957
[laughing]

618
00:34:51,958 --> 00:34:53,958
- Peace.
- Peace.

619
00:34:55,625 --> 00:34:57,540
This is good.

620
00:34:57,541 --> 00:35:00,457
This summer, I wanted
to try new things, you know?

621
00:35:00,458 --> 00:35:02,457
Live like it's the last summer
I'll ever have.

622
00:35:02,458 --> 00:35:03,749
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

623
00:35:03,750 --> 00:35:05,958
- That's a good way to live.
- Mm-hmm.

624
00:35:07,375 --> 00:35:10,040
So what's next on your list?

625
00:35:10,041 --> 00:35:13,540
To go to bed without brushing your teeth?

626
00:35:13,541 --> 00:35:15,665
Never.

627
00:35:15,666 --> 00:35:19,457
Or to... not eat your vegetables?

628
00:35:19,458 --> 00:35:20,833
Maybe.

629
00:35:21,958 --> 00:35:24,333
Or to make out with a hot stranger?

630
00:35:25,833 --> 00:35:27,832
I could pretend you're hot.

631
00:35:27,833 --> 00:35:29,833
♪ ♪

632
00:35:53,791 --> 00:35:55,750
♪ ♪

633
00:36:11,333 --> 00:36:13,333
[ringtone playing in distance]

634
00:36:25,416 --> 00:36:26,833
[ringtone continues]

635
00:36:36,666 --> 00:36:37,874
Everything okay?

636
00:36:37,875 --> 00:36:39,458
[chuckles] Yeah.

637
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,208
You look beautiful.

638
00:36:48,083 --> 00:36:49,833
You know, you're not that moody.

639
00:36:51,833 --> 00:36:53,457
What?

640
00:36:53,458 --> 00:36:55,708
Just something Amara said.

641
00:37:00,375 --> 00:37:02,791
Come on. I should get you back.

642
00:37:06,291 --> 00:37:07,500
Yeah.

643
00:37:16,708 --> 00:37:17,916
[engine shuts off]

644
00:37:27,541 --> 00:37:29,665
I'm sorry.

645
00:37:29,666 --> 00:37:31,499
I feel like I upset you.

646
00:37:31,500 --> 00:37:33,582
I'm just stressed.

647
00:37:33,583 --> 00:37:35,415
It's about work.

648
00:37:35,416 --> 00:37:36,874
I have a lot going on.

649
00:37:36,875 --> 00:37:37,958
I know.

650
00:37:40,375 --> 00:37:42,125
Can I give you my number?

651
00:37:44,125 --> 00:37:46,290
I... would like that.

652
00:37:46,291 --> 00:37:49,582
- [chuckling]
- If you didn't, I'd feel used.

653
00:37:49,583 --> 00:37:50,500
I'll trade you.

654
00:37:58,125 --> 00:37:59,208
There.

655
00:38:02,625 --> 00:38:04,125
I'll call you.

656
00:38:05,625 --> 00:38:06,958
Okay.

657
00:38:11,250 --> 00:38:12,458
Good night, Oriah.

658
00:38:15,208 --> 00:38:16,416
Good night.

659
00:38:19,500 --> 00:38:20,832
[engine starts]

660
00:38:20,833 --> 00:38:22,790
[insects trilling]

661
00:38:22,791 --> 00:38:24,791
[motorcycle approaching]

662
00:38:31,125 --> 00:38:32,457
[engine shuts off]

663
00:38:32,458 --> 00:38:34,165
You didn't even kiss her good night.

664
00:38:34,166 --> 00:38:36,500
[pensive music playing]

665
00:38:42,750 --> 00:38:45,290
Look, I don't have your money yet, okay?

666
00:38:45,291 --> 00:38:47,457
But I'm working on it.

667
00:38:47,458 --> 00:38:48,707
I'll get it for you.

668
00:38:48,708 --> 00:38:50,708
[grunting]

669
00:38:53,208 --> 00:38:55,416
[coughing]

670
00:38:58,375 --> 00:38:59,582
Of course you'll get it.

671
00:38:59,583 --> 00:39:00,999
[groans, coughs]

672
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,832
'Cause if you don't,

673
00:39:02,833 --> 00:39:04,791
I'll get it from your girlfriend.

674
00:39:05,833 --> 00:39:07,082
She must be pretty rich

675
00:39:07,083 --> 00:39:09,040
if she's staying
in a place like this, huh?

676
00:39:09,041 --> 00:39:10,582
[panting]

677
00:39:10,583 --> 00:39:12,624
[Julian groans]

678
00:39:12,625 --> 00:39:14,040
[grunts, coughs]

679
00:39:14,041 --> 00:39:15,833
[laughing]

680
00:39:18,291 --> 00:39:20,207
<i>Vámonos.</i>

681
00:39:20,208 --> 00:39:21,415
[groans]

682
00:39:21,416 --> 00:39:22,957
[panting]

683
00:39:22,958 --> 00:39:24,708
[car doors closing]

684
00:39:27,208 --> 00:39:31,124
[Isolde] <i>Just finalizing the deal
with the local landowner, but the hotel</i>

685
00:39:31,125 --> 00:39:32,957
will be built.

686
00:39:32,958 --> 00:39:34,749
So, let's talk about you.

687
00:39:34,750 --> 00:39:36,207
Did you take your pills this morning?

688
00:39:36,208 --> 00:39:38,415
Um...

689
00:39:38,416 --> 00:39:39,874
[Ry stammers]

690
00:39:39,875 --> 00:39:41,707
Uh, I'm just still
getting used to the new meds.

691
00:39:41,708 --> 00:39:43,290
You know how it is.

692
00:39:43,291 --> 00:39:44,750
Yeah, I'm sorry.

693
00:39:46,083 --> 00:39:48,207
I've been hanging out with Amara.

694
00:39:48,208 --> 00:39:49,415
From the front desk.

695
00:39:49,416 --> 00:39:50,874
Oh, right, yeah, yeah.

696
00:39:50,875 --> 00:39:52,040
And some of her friends.

697
00:39:52,041 --> 00:39:55,500
Well, as long as you're not falling
in love with some hot Spaniard.

698
00:39:56,500 --> 00:39:57,833
[chuckles]

699
00:39:58,875 --> 00:40:00,540
- What? Already?
- [chuckles]

700
00:40:00,541 --> 00:40:02,165
Okay. I'm not even gonna ask.

701
00:40:02,166 --> 00:40:05,207
But if you could peel yourself away
for a couple days,

702
00:40:05,208 --> 00:40:06,582
I could really use your help.

703
00:40:06,583 --> 00:40:10,082
Have your people call my people,
and maybe we'll figure something out.

704
00:40:10,083 --> 00:40:11,582
I'll do that.

705
00:40:11,583 --> 00:40:13,958
- [band playing flamenco music]
- [singer speaking Spanish]

706
00:40:23,750 --> 00:40:25,916
[singing in Spanish]

707
00:40:27,375 --> 00:40:30,083
[talking indistinctly under music]

708
00:40:37,375 --> 00:40:39,499
[chef talking indistinctly under music]

709
00:40:39,500 --> 00:40:40,874
Mmm.

710
00:40:40,875 --> 00:40:42,875
[talking indistinctly under music]

711
00:40:45,083 --> 00:40:46,458
I love the artichoke.

712
00:40:48,291 --> 00:40:51,250
[conversing indistinctly under music]

713
00:40:56,416 --> 00:40:58,541
- [song continues]
- [shoes tapping rhythmically]

714
00:41:03,875 --> 00:41:05,833
[Isolde speaking Spanish]

715
00:41:09,375 --> 00:41:11,375
[talking indistinctly under music]

716
00:41:14,916 --> 00:41:17,749
- [song ends]
- [woman] <i>¡Olé! ¡Olé!</i>

717
00:41:17,750 --> 00:41:18,874
- Incredible. Oh, my--
- [song resumes]

718
00:41:18,875 --> 00:41:19,790
[singer exclaiming in Spanish]

719
00:41:19,791 --> 00:41:20,707
- Oh.
- Oh.

720
00:41:20,708 --> 00:41:21,749
Oh, my God! Our turn.

721
00:41:21,750 --> 00:41:23,707
- [laughing]
- Get it, Mom.

722
00:41:23,708 --> 00:41:25,624
[both laughing]

723
00:41:25,625 --> 00:41:27,583
[singer continues exclaiming in Spanish]

724
00:41:31,291 --> 00:41:33,291
[song fades]

725
00:41:37,208 --> 00:41:38,665
Ooh, thank God. There you are.

726
00:41:38,666 --> 00:41:41,999
Will you come with me to a bar downtown
for a Tinder date?

727
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:43,207
[laughs] No.

728
00:41:43,208 --> 00:41:45,582
No, I can't come on a date with you.

729
00:41:45,583 --> 00:41:48,457
Yes. You have to be my safety net
in case she's a serial killer.

730
00:41:48,458 --> 00:41:50,540
You can be our third wheel.

731
00:41:50,541 --> 00:41:52,374
We'll be one big happy tricycle.

732
00:41:52,375 --> 00:41:55,875
Unless of course we get to the good stuff,
then I can be quite possessive.

733
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:59,375
Go, change! I want to hear
all about Julian the other night.

734
00:42:00,375 --> 00:42:01,707
- [chuckles]
- Go.

735
00:42:01,708 --> 00:42:03,707
So, who is this girl?

736
00:42:03,708 --> 00:42:07,624
Prisha. She's a medical student
visiting from London.

737
00:42:07,625 --> 00:42:09,082
How long is she here for?

738
00:42:09,083 --> 00:42:10,832
Uh, three weeks, I think.

739
00:42:10,833 --> 00:42:12,707
Oh, that's not long.

740
00:42:12,708 --> 00:42:14,582
What if you catch feelings?

741
00:42:14,583 --> 00:42:16,540
Just because something
doesn't last forever

742
00:42:16,541 --> 00:42:18,957
doesn't mean it's not worth experiencing.

743
00:42:18,958 --> 00:42:21,915
And anyway, this is a tourist island.

744
00:42:21,916 --> 00:42:24,915
- People come and go.
- Hmm.

745
00:42:24,916 --> 00:42:28,583
I mean, you won't be here forever,
and you still made out with J.

746
00:42:29,666 --> 00:42:31,707
- Ah! Knew it.
- [laughs]

747
00:42:31,708 --> 00:42:33,540
Locked lips with a scoundrel.

748
00:42:33,541 --> 00:42:36,249
It was just one kiss.

749
00:42:36,250 --> 00:42:38,125
And I haven't heard from him since.

750
00:42:39,125 --> 00:42:40,915
Oh.

751
00:42:40,916 --> 00:42:42,790
Are you that bad of a kisser?

752
00:42:42,791 --> 00:42:44,332
No.

753
00:42:44,333 --> 00:42:47,249
What? I'm just saying.
One kiss then nothing?

754
00:42:47,250 --> 00:42:48,499
No tongue?

755
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:50,540
[gasps] Too much tongue?

756
00:42:50,541 --> 00:42:51,915
- Oh, God.
- [laughs]

757
00:42:51,916 --> 00:42:53,416
["Sufre Mamón" playing]

758
00:42:53,916 --> 00:42:55,874
[singing in Spanish to music]

759
00:42:55,875 --> 00:42:57,875
[lively chatter]

760
00:43:02,333 --> 00:43:06,374
Well, you've already seen him naked,
so you know what you are getting.

761
00:43:06,375 --> 00:43:07,707
Okay. Oh.

762
00:43:07,708 --> 00:43:09,749
There she is.

763
00:43:09,750 --> 00:43:11,707
- Do you want me to hang back?
- No, no.

764
00:43:11,708 --> 00:43:13,540
She could be dangerous.

765
00:43:13,541 --> 00:43:15,207
- [chuckles]
- Just...

766
00:43:15,208 --> 00:43:16,250
[Amara sighs]

767
00:43:18,291 --> 00:43:20,040
Uh, Prisha?

768
